A||||6||Phil||Which temp. sensor is which?||||1||
Z||000000||Phil||06-27-2001||06:30 PM||||Kinda new to this 4 banger thing, 88 coupe What temp sensor is the one in the head by the thermostat housing(not the one in the housing)? I'm leaning to fan switch but I'm not sure. Just to be fully informed- what's the one in the 'stat housing and the one in the intake manifold?||||reg||1
Z||000001||beachbomb||06-27-2001||06:51 PM||||Hey, the one in the therm housing is the temp gauge, the one pointing towards the back of the drivers seat is the fan sensor, and the other one is for the ECM..hope this helps..jim(2 '84 Indys)||||reg||1
Z||000002||Phil||06-27-2001||08:23 PM||||Guess 88's are different the one by the 'stat housing is verticle(points toward the deck lid). It's a 2 wire jobbie.||||reg||1
Z||000003||beachbomb||06-27-2001||08:58 PM||||Hey Phil, my guess they are still the same ones, just different positions. The one on my therm housing is the temp guage for the dash..Jim||||reg||1
Z||000004||Songman||06-27-2001||09:02 PM||||This helps me too... My temp gauge doesn't work on the Indy... I have wondered but never bothered to find out.<P>What did you get, Phil? 88 coupe, I know.. but we wanna see!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/songman_1.gif">  <BR><A HREF="http://members.home.com/tnfieros" TARGET=_blank>Tennessee Fiero Owners</A><p>[This message has been edited by Songman (edited 06-27-2001).]||||reg||1
